e-detective-preventive walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the control-selection rationale + placement map + tuning procedure
authored and self-reviewed in-session against NIST SP 800-94 (IDS/IPS types and
management considerations) and the Honeynet Project's deployment knowledge.

Scope: fictional Meridian Analytics (180 staff, continued from e-iam). SOC model:
2 analysts + contracted MDR nights/weekends. Crown jewels: customer DB, CI/CD.
Artifacts authored (all fictional, labeled):
  - Control selection: 5 risks → type/placement/tuning-owner (IDS passive at
    ingress + IPS inline at egress; low-interaction honeypot inside each trust
    zone; DLP detect-then-block at email/web/endpoint; allow-listing on prod
    servers; IdP anomaly detection).
  - Placement decisions with reasons: inline-only-at-egress policy set by the
    recorded incident of the customer-portal false block; honeypot at never-
    assigned addresses (any touch = suspicious); DLP monitor-only 30 days
    before blocking.
  - Tuning procedure: per-control owner + cadence + measured FP rate;
    quarterly review (fired/real/environmental changes/retirements).

